- op: discuss  # ee1e
  at: '2026-04-09T00:56:10Z'  # ee1e
  by: agent  # ee1e
  actor: jgstern_agent  # ee1e
  clock: 10  # ee1e
  nonce: ee1e  # ee1e
  message: "[Blast radius analysis for Option B — add is_test boolean to FileClassification]\n\nINVESTIGATION COMPLETE. Verdict: MEDIUM scope, surgical, additive, low risk.\n\nPRODUCTION CODE TOUCHPOINTS (4 files, all small):\n\n(1) packages/hypergumbo-core/src/hypergumbo_core/supply_chain.py — add is_test: bool field to FileClassification dataclass (~lines 92-99). Set it during test-pattern detection at lines 304-314 (workspace-package-root branch) and lines 326-331 (non-workspace branch). The detection logic ALREADY exists; we are exposing it as a separate axis instead of folding it into tier.\n\n(2) packages/hypergumbo-core/src/hypergumbo_core/ir.py — add is_test_file: bool = False to Symbol dataclass (~lines 243-249). Update Symbol.to_dict() at lines 278-282 to include 'is_test_file' inside the nested supply_chain dict. Update Symbol.from_dict() at lines 311-312 to reconstruct via supply_chain.get('is_test_file', False).\n\n(3) packages/hypergumbo-core/src/hypergumbo_core/cli.py:4632 — single assignment line: symbol.is_test_file = classification.is_test, alongside the existing supply_chain_tier assignment.\n\n(4) packages/hypergumbo-core/src/hypergumbo_core/sketch.py:4883 — same single assignment in the parallel propagation path (sketch builds its own symbol decorations).\n\nOPTIONAL: schema.py SCHEMA_VERSION bump 0.2.2 → 0.2.3 (additive field, so technically a patch bump). docs/schema.json may regenerate automatically depending on hooks; manual edit unlikely needed.\n\nEXISTING test-detection mechanisms (we are NOT introducing a new concept):\n- _is_test_node() in cli.py:1173 — already used by hypergumbo explain -x to filter test callers/callees\n- _TEST_PATH_RE — already used by bakeoff-deep tier-slice query selection (entries.txt filter)\n- TEST_FILE_PATTERNS / TEST_DIR_PATTERNS in supply_chain.py — the same regexes that classify_file already runs to demote tier\n- --exclude-tests CLI flag already wired up at multiple call sites in cli.py (lines 3558, 3889, 4061+) for slice/symbols/explain\nThe new is_test_file field is a structured exposure of what these already detect; it lets consumers query the bit directly instead of re-running regex on paths or scanning annotations.\n\nTEST SUITE TOUCHPOINTS (~10 test files, ~60-80 assertion changes):\n\n- packages/hypergumbo-core/tests/test_supply_chain.py — TestTestFileClassification (~19 cases) and TestFuzzBenchClassification (~9 cases) need is_test=True assertions added alongside existing tier assertions. None of them need to flip — the tier semantics are unchanged, we are just adding a parallel assertion. Mechanical edit.\n- packages/hypergumbo-core/tests/test_ir.py — Symbol round-trip tests (~10) need is_test_file field round-tripped through to_dict/from_dict. Mechanical.\n- packages/hypergumbo-core/tests/test_sketch.py — ~4 Symbol construction sites need the new field defaulted (or explicitly passed False).\n- packages/hypergumbo-core/tests/test_slice_tier_filter.py — make_symbol() helper signature needs is_test_file parameter, ~10 call sites.\n- test_compact.py, test_ranking.py, test_entrypoints.py — minor Symbol construction updates (3+ files, a handful of sites each).\n\nNEW TESTS TO ADD:\n- supply_chain test: classify_file on a Go _test.go file inside a workspace package_root → assert tier=2 (unchanged) AND is_test=True (new).\n- supply_chain test: classify_file on a non-test .go file in the same package → tier=1 AND is_test=False.\n- ir test: Symbol(is_test_file=True) round-trips through to_dict/from_dict cleanly.\n- cli/sketch propagation test: a fixture repo with both test and non-test files → assert produced behavior map has node.supply_chain.is_test_file matching expectations.\n\nCONSUMERS THAT MIGHT WANT TO UPGRADE (none required, all opt-in):\n- bakeoff-deep tier-slice query (scripts/bakeoff-deep) currently filters via _TEST_PATH_RE at the entries-selection stage. After this lands it could optionally compose 'tier=2 AND NOT is_test_file' at the slice-result inspection stage to give a clean 'real third-party deps' answer. The original WI rationale.\n- hypergumbo  # ee1e
    slice --max-tier consumers could optionally add an --exclude-tests flag (or compose with the existing one) to get 'production code only' answers without relying on tier alone.\n- Sketch ordering, centrality ranking, orphan-rate metrics: NO automatic behavior change. They keep using tier as today. Anyone who wants to compose is_test_file into their query must opt in explicitly.\n\nHIDDEN COUPLING RISKS — none material. Tier counts in the behavior map profile, centrality rankings, sketch ordering, and bakeoff metrics all stay byte-for-byte identical with the additive change. The only behavioral shift would come from a consumer voluntarily switching its query to use the new field.\n\nTOTAL TOUCH COUNT: 4-5 production files, ~10 test files, ~60-80 assertion/parameter changes, no schema migration, no new CLI flags (the existing --exclude-tests covers the user-facing case). One PR.\n\nASSESSMENT: this is the cheapest path that solves the bakeoff problem AND preserves the 89154fa20 'tests are not production code' framing AND avoids unwinding any of the ~28 existing TestTestFileClassification assertions. Strictly additive. Low merge risk.\n\nAwaiting your go-ahead to proceed with implementation. I would ship it as a single feature PR, not split it. After it lands, the bakeoff-deep tier-slice query upgrade is a separate small follow-up PR (touches scripts/bakeoff-deep only)."  # ee1e
